<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Baol</h1><p class="st-meta">1555 CE – 1894 CE · capital Lambaye</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Wolof and Serer kingdom of central Senegal, often united with Cayor, where Amadou Bamba later founded the holy city of Touba.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baol">Baol</a> was a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a> that broke away in the mid-16th century, following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor's</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-danki">Danki</a> in 1549. Its ruler, the Teigne, was chosen from royal lineages with ties to both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> families, and the capital was at Lambaye.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Teigne ruled with titled chiefs and a slave soldiery over a mixed population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> farmers growing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groundnut">groundnuts</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baol">Baol</a> was frequently united with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cayor">Cayor</a> under one ruler; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lat-sukaabe-fall">Lat Sukaabe Fall</a> held both thrones around 1700. Baol's coastal towns traded with the French and Portuguese.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> established control over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baol">Baol</a> in the 1880s and 1890s and absorbed it into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-senegal">French Senegal</a>. In 1887 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadou-bamba">Amadou Bamba</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touba">Touba</a> in Baol, and the region became the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mouride-brotherhood">Mouride brotherhood</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-baol.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Baol" width="320" height="241"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Baol_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1555 CE – 1894 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lambaye</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lat Sukaabe Fall</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam and Serer religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Wolof and Serer</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/senegal">Senegal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Baol, Bawol</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=kingdom-of-baol" aria-label="Kingdom of Baol on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4228 1627 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Baol lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4548 1883L4544 1864M4548 1883L4587 1861M4548 1883L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4544 1864h0M4587 1861h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4548 1883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4548 1883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lambaye. <a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=kingdom-of-baol">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
